{"at":"2026-10-30T15:50:15.782Z","component":"Thunderbird Account Hub input property documentation","evidence":["7c9d75e8ee9ee130007c4f777e45af100aea4737714736e4d8a099ca28544233","de20858e68a248f45b5782d79bf0713decc0b34c09eee63d49f0c9d47be8982c","e1be552d935bd74ca8c25764b230918f465882d36fc03312691287e4b52c8725","e83e419cf1e80d5b4f18a3d0295e02d91161d177e126e94685eb22d0d9bd8418","fab2c6e41d8a9f60d6a270c906cc209a09db951561e27a633a5af62369894366"],"id":"272c66a7d1dc72a49766a6b6bdc4b041b4d02bfc7e3349f22f8a734781af62ec","kind":"lesson","paths":["mail/components/accountcreation/content/widgets/account-hub-input.mjs","mail/components/accountcreation/content/widgets/email-manual-config-form.mjs","mail/components/accountcreation/templates/accountHubEmailManualConfigFormTemplate.inc.xhtml"],"quotes":[{"id":"e1be552d935bd74ca8c25764b230918f465882d36fc03312691287e4b52c8725","text":"* The value of the input element."},{"id":"e1be552d935bd74ca8c25764b230918f465882d36fc03312691287e4b52c8725","text":"this.#input.value = newValue;"},{"id":"e1be552d935bd74ca8c25764b230918f465882d36fc03312691287e4b52c8725","text":"return this.#input.valueAsNumber;"},{"id":"7c9d75e8ee9ee130007c4f777e45af100aea4737714736e4d8a099ca28544233","text":"this.#input = this.querySelector(\"input\");"},{"id":"fab2c6e41d8a9f60d6a270c906cc209a09db951561e27a633a5af62369894366","text":"this.#incomingPort = this.querySelector(\"#manualIncomingPort\");"},{"id":"e83e419cf1e80d5b4f18a3d0295e02d91161d177e126e94685eb22d0d9bd8418","text":"id=\"manualIncomingPort\""},{"id":"de20858e68a248f45b5782d79bf0713decc0b34c09eee63d49f0c9d47be8982c","text":"config.incoming.port = this.#incomingPort.valueAsNumber;"}],"repository":"thunderbird","source":{"basis":"Quoted evidence supports the claim; its interpretation still needs current-source checks.","revision":"0b93f0f7a926ed94c8a0646f18b6734ec7cc0f6d","sourceAt":"2026-10-05T22:44:59Z","type":"extraction"},"status":"supported","supersedes":[],"text":"The component describes the string value getter and setter with one @type property comment and marks getter-only valueAsNumber read-only. Both delegate to the internal native input. The modern manual-config port template instantiates this custom component, and its controller writes value before reading valueAsNumber. Accessor bodies are retained; declaration order changes. The claimed documentation-build repair is historical and was not run here.","title":"AccountHubInput documents its paired value accessors as one property","version":1,"visibility":"shared"}
